    "Full API spec": "Module crud_system/errors.py:\n- class ValidationError(Exception): raised by validation.py validate_name when input name is invalid.\n- class DuplicateNameError(Exception): raised by Repository on name uniqueness violation during create/update.\n- class NotFoundError(Exception): raised by Repository when get/update/delete targets a missing ID.\n- class PaginationError(Exception): raised by search.paginate for negative offset or negative non-None limit.\n\nModule crud_system/types.py:\n- class Item:\n  - Fields: id:int, name:str, created_at:float, updated_at:float.\n  - Semantics: stable identifier assigned by Repository; created_at set on creation; updated_at updated on updates.\n- class AuditEvent:\n  - Fields: op:str, item_id:int, item_name:str, ts:float.\n  - Semantics: append-only records created by AuditTrail.log with explicit timestamp provided by Service.\n- class Page:\n  - Non-generic class (no Generic, no TypeVar). Fields: items:list[Item], total:int, limit:int, offset:int.\n  - Semantics: describes a deterministic slice of a larger item list. Page annotations must not use subscriptions like Page[Item].\n\nModule crud_system/clock.py:\n- class FixedClock:\n  - __init__(base:float=100.0, step:float=10.0) -> None. Stores current time and step.\n  - now(self) -> float: returns current value then advances internal state by step.\n  - Semantics: deterministic time; must be consumed exclusively by Service for create/update/delete; a single operation must never advance the clock twice.\n\nModule crud_system/validation.py:\n- validate_name(name: str) -> None:\n  - Behavior: raises ValidationError if name is invalid (e.g., None, empty, whitespace-only, or not a str); otherwise returns None.\n  - Deterministic and pure; has no side effects.\n\nModule crud_system/repository.py:\n- Imports: from .errors import DuplicateNameError, NotFoundError (direct import required).\n- class Repository:\n  - Internal state: _items: dict[int, Item]; _name_index: dict[str, int]; _next_id:int starting at 1.\n  - create(self, name: str, ts: float) -> Item:\n    - Assigns a stable new id; enforces name uniqueness via _name_index; raises DuplicateNameError on conflict; sets created_at and updated_at to ts.\n  - get(self, item_id: int) -> Item:\n    - Returns the Item or raises NotFoundError if missing.\n  - update(self, item_id: int, name: str, ts: float) -> Item:\n    - Ensures item exists; enforces name uniqueness if changing name; updates name and updated_at=ts; raises DuplicateNameError or NotFoundError accordingly.\n  - delete(self, item_id: int) -> None:\n    - Removes the item and name index entry; raises NotFoundError if missing.\n  - list_items(self) -> list[Item]:\n    - Returns items sorted by name for deterministic ordering.\n  - exists_name(self, name: str) -> bool:\n    - Returns True if name is present in _name_index; False otherwise.\n\nModule crud_system/search.py:\n- Imports: from .types import Item, Page and from .errors import PaginationError.\n- paginate(items: list[Item], limit: int|None = None, offset: int = 0) -> Page:\n  - Validates: offset must be >= 0; limit is None or >= 0; else raises PaginationError.\n  - Slicing: effective_limit = len(items) - offset if limit is None else limit; selected = items[offset: offset + effective_limit].\n  - Returns Page(items=selected, total=len(items), limit=effective_limit, offset=offset).\n  - Contract: No generics; signature exactly as above; return annotation is Page (not Page[Item]).\n\nModule crud_system/audit.py:\n- class AuditTrail:\n  - Constructor: AuditTrail() takes no clock; maintains an in-memory list of AuditEvent.\n  - log(self, op: str, item_id: int, item_name: str, ts: float) -> None:\n    - Appends an AuditEvent(op, item_id, item_name, ts) to internal list.\n  - events(self) -> list[AuditEvent]:\n    - Returns a copy or stable view of the recorded audit events.\n\nModule crud_system/service.py:\n- class Service:\n  - Constructor: Service(repo: Repository, audit: AuditTrail, clock: FixedClock).\n  - create(self, name: str) -> Item:\n    - Calls validate_name; calls clock.now() exactly once to get ts; repo.create(name, ts) to create entity; audit.log(\"create\", item_id, name, ts); returns created Item.\n  - read(self, item_id: int) -> Item:\n    - Delegates to repo.get(item_id); no clock usage.\n  - update(self, item_id: int, name: str) -> Item:\n    - Calls validate_name; ts = clock.now() exactly once; repo.update(item_id, name, ts); audit.log(\"update\", item_id, name, ts); returns updated Item.\n  - delete(self, item_id: int) -> None:\n    - ts = clock.now() exactly once; fetch existing item via repo.get to capture name; repo.delete(item_id); audit.log(\"delete\", item_id, item_name, ts); returns None.\n  - search(self, name_contains: str|None = None, limit: int|None = None, offset: int = 0) -> Page:\n    - Gets items via repo.list_items(); applies optional filter by substring match in name if name_contains is not None; sorts by name deterministically; returns paginate(filtered_items, limit, offset).\n  - audit_events(self) -> list[AuditEvent]:\n    - Returns audit.events().\n  - Ownership: Service is the only component calling FixedClock.now; each mutation operation must call now() exactly once and reuse the same ts for both entity timestamps and audit trail.\n\nModule crud_system/__init__.py:\n- Exports canonical API only: Item, AuditEvent, Page, FixedClock, Repository, AuditTrail, Service, paginate, ValidationError, DuplicateNameError, NotFoundError, PaginationError. No extraneous exports or side effects.\n\nModule Main.py:\n- Thin demo: constructs Repository, FixedClock(base=100.0, step=10.0), AuditTrail, Service; performs a bounded sequence (e.g., create, update, search, delete) and exits; no interactive loops; deterministic.\n\nTests tests/test_main.py:\n- Exactly three pytest tests:\n  1) CRUD timestamps: assert create at 100.0 and update at 110.0 using FixedClock(100.0, 10.0); for each operation, item timestamps and audit timestamp are identical; clock is called once per operation by Service.\n  2) Duplicate and NotFound: creating a duplicate name raises DuplicateNameError; reading or deleting a missing ID raises NotFoundError.\n  3) Pagination and audit timing: create Alpha, Beta, Gamma; search with limit=2, offset=1 returns names [\"Beta\", \"Gamma\"]; audit timestamps equal [100.0, 110.0, 120.0].\n\nAllowed import/include directions:\n- errors.py and types.py are foundational and must not import downstream modules.\n- repository.py imports only types and errors; directly imports DuplicateNameError and NotFoundError.\n- search.py imports Item, Page from .types and PaginationError from .errors directly.\n- audit.py imports only types.\n- service.py imports repository, audit, clock, validation, search, and types; is the sole consumer of FixedClock.now.\n- __init__.py re-exports only canonical symbols from submodules; tests import only through this canonical surface.\n- Page must remain non-generic; forbid Page[Item] and any Generic subscriptions in public annotations.\n",
    "Shared Knowledge": "The repository is a Python 3.10 package with deterministic CRUD and pagination semantics. Files and responsibilities:\n- crud_system/errors.py defines all custom exceptions and is directly imported where exceptions are raised.\n- crud_system/types.py owns Item, AuditEvent, and a non-generic Page class with fields items:list[Item], total:int, limit:int, offset:int.\n- crud_system/clock.py defines FixedClock; only Service calls now().\n- crud_system/validation.py provides validate_name which raises ValidationError for invalid inputs.\n- crud_system/repository.py implements in-memory CRUD with stable IDs and name uniqueness; directly imports DuplicateNameError and NotFoundError.\n- crud_system/search.py implements paginate(items:list[Item], limit:int|None=None, offset:int=0)->Page; imports Item and Page directly from .types and PaginationError from .errors; no generics.\n- crud_system/audit.py implements AuditTrail with explicit timestamp logging; does not call any clock.\n- crud_system/service.py orchestrates operations and enforces the single clock call per mutation; search filters optional substring, sorts by name, and paginates.\n- crud_system/__init__.py provides the canonical exports consumed by tests and Main.py.\n- Main.py is a thin demo entrypoint; no IO loops; deterministic and headless.\n- tests/test_main.py contains exactly three pytest tests importing only from crud_system canonical exports; they verify timestamps, errors, pagination, and audit behavior.\nAll modules avoid circular dependencies; foundational modules do not import higher layers. Tests must import under Python 3.10 successfully before executing any assertions.",
    "Execution Protocol": "Test command: python -m pytest -q. Single test target: tests/test_main.py with exactly three tests. Runtime entry: Main.py provides a bounded, non-interactive demonstration. No network access or OS-specific behavior. Additional files do not alter protocol files. The project is deterministic and headless; tests use only canonical exports from crud_system.",
